# Copy to `.env.local` and replace the placeholder with your real Web3Forms access key.
# Do NOT commit your real `.env.local` to source control.
# Example:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=sk_live_abcdef1234567890

NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=your_web3forms_access_key_here

# Notes:
# - For local dev, copy this file to `.env.local` and set the real key.
# - For production (Vercel/Netlify/Cloud), add the same variable in your host's Environment Variables section and redeploy.
# - If you prefer not to expose the key client-side, ask me and I can implement a small server-side proxy/API route.
 
# If you want server-side forwarding (recommended) set this instead and keep it non-public:
# WEB3FORMS_API_KEY=your_web3forms_api_key_here

# When using the server-side proxy (app/api/contact), the client will call `/api/contact` and
# the server will forward the request to Web3Forms using `WEB3FORMS_API_KEY` (kept secret).
